  "total_performance_visual_contract": "Rows are model families/checkpoint variants. Columns are ordered migration fixed pathway, migration self-relaxed, and sliding. Color is the raw predicted barrier/peak energy in eV on one global PowerNorm display scale (gamma=0.40; lower values yellow and higher values purple); circle radius encodes absolute predicted-energy error in eV. Aggregate trained-family values are means over seeds 123/234/345; each trained-family circle is split into one wedge per seed. Rows follow Scratch 600K then MultiT, FT 600K then MultiT, and Foundation checkpoints. Scratch, Fine-tuning, and Foundation use compact vertical bracket groups. The companion seed-expanded figure has 15 rows: 12 trained seed units and three single-checkpoint Foundation rows."
